{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1788975784,"nonce":"586OTQ3Ukr7MwWM0geKRMGI5vu8=","title":"promotion_wants_full_module lowers without callees but asks the cache with callees_visible","message":"`llvm/air.rs` lowers against a `without_callees()` module while asking the\n`AirConfigKey` cache under `callees_visible: true`. Whichever caller reaches a\nfindex first therefore decides the shared standard entry for everyone.\n\nBoth sides of an OSR transfer must lower under the same `AirConfigKey`: the entry\naddresses slots as `value_reg(v) * 8` with no bounds check, and the site is a pc\ninto the serialized OPTIMIZED opcode array. Same key means both sides get the\nsame `Arc\u003cOptimized\u003e`, and that identity IS the safety mechanism.\n\nThis one is wrong today, independent of any level work.","files":null}]}